    context: "The council forbade the apostles to speak in Jesus' name, and they answered that they could not stop. Daniel's friends refused to worship the image, saying they trusted God whether or not he delivered them. Daniel continued to pray openly despite the decree. Such refusals were not rebellions against the state as a whole, but acts of faithfulness to God in specific matters. Today, believers may face laws that require participation in idolatry, injustice, falsehood or harm to others, or forbid worship and evangelism.",
