    summary: "Matthew 5:10-12 declares blessed those persecuted for righteousness. First Peter 4:12-19 tells believers not to be surprised at the fiery trial. Romans 8:35-39 says nothing can separate us from Christ's love. Acts 7:54-60 shows Stephen praying for his killers. Hebrews 13:3 urges remembering the mistreated. This lesson helps believers prepare for opposition and support those who suffer, in a spirit of faith and non-retaliation.",
    scripture: ["Matthew 5:10-12", "1 Peter 4:12-19"], more: ["Romans 8:35-39", "Acts 7:54-60", "Hebrews 13:3"], memory: "Matthew 5:10",
