    activity: "Read John 18:33-37 and Luke 4:1-13. Discuss the temptation to gain power by compromise. Role-play a dialogue about the proper roles of church and state. Pray.",
    takeHome: "Read John 18, Matthew 22, Luke 4 and Acts 4 and 5. Write a short statement of how you understand the church's relationship to government. Memorise John 18:36.",
    prayer: "Pray that the church will keep faith with Christ's kingdom and speak wisely to society. Pray for freedom of conscience for all.",
    teacher: "Remain strictly non-partisan and note that Christian traditions differ on church and state. Avoid current partisan examples. Respect local laws on the activities of religious bodies. Be sensitive to learners from minority religions or oppressive contexts.",
